{"id":"0883e36f1192a12f","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-first-passage.md","title":"First Passage Time","display":"df-first-passage — First Passage Time","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-first-passage","aliases":["58-df-first-passage","First Passage Time"],"display":"df-first-passage — First Passage Time","depends_on":["[[../batch16/58-df-omega.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-first-passage"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-first-passage</span><span>First Passage Time</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-first-passage — First Passage Time"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5045d216c83e75cb\" href=\"?note=5045d216c83e75cb\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-omega.md\">../batch16/58-df-omega.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\">\\((\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (probability space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\in\\{\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\}\">\\(T\\in\\{\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\}\\)</span> (time set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(E,\\mathcal E)\">\\((E,\\mathcal E)\\)</span> (measurable state space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\\in(E^\\Omega)^T\">\\(X\\in(E^\\Omega)^T\\)</span> (stochastic process)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\in\\mathcal E\">\\(A\\in\\mathcal E\\)</span> (target set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_A\\in(T\\cup\\{\\infty\\})^\\Omega\">\\(\\tau_A\\in(T\\cup\\{\\infty\\})^\\Omega\\)</span> (candidate first-passage time)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{FirstPassageTime}_S(\\tau_A,X,A)\">\\(\\operatorname{FirstPassageTime}_S(\\tau_A,X,A)\\)</span> (first-passage-time predicate, 本文件定义)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}first\\text{-}passage} \\vdash \\operatorname{FirstPassageTime}_S(\\tau_A,X,A) \\leftrightarrow T\\in\\{\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\}\\land X\\in(E^\\Omega)^T\\land A\\in\\mathcal E\\land\\tau_A\\in(T\\cup\\{\\infty\\})^\\Omega\\land\\forall\\omega_0\\in\\Omega\\;\\bigl(\\tau_A(\\omega_0)=\\inf(\\{t\\in T:X(t)(\\omega_0)\\in A\\}\\cup\\{\\infty\\})\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}first\\text{-}passage} \\vdash \\operatorname{FirstPassageTime}_S(\\tau_A,X,A) \\leftrightarrow T\\in\\{\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\}\\land X\\in(E^\\Omega)^T\\land A\\in\\mathcal E\\land\\tau_A\\in(T\\cup\\{\\infty\\})^\\Omega\\land\\forall\\omega_0\\in\\Omega\\;\\bigl(\\tau_A(\\omega_0)=\\inf(\\{t\\in T:X(t)(\\omega_0)\\in A\\}\\cup\\{\\infty\\})\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>First passage: time to first reach a set; fundamental in stochastic processes</li>\n<li>The displayed clause defines the hitting-time functional. It is a stopping time only after an adapted filtration and suitable measurability/path hypotheses are supplied, so no unconditional stopping-time predicate is imported here.</li>\n<li>Dirichlet characterizations of expected hitting times and gambler's-ruin probabilities are theorems requiring generator, boundary, and process assumptions; they are not defining clauses.</li>\n<li>Wald: sequential analysis; stopping rule and likelihood ratio</li>\n<li>Lévy: arcsine laws for first passage of Brownian motion</li>\n<li>Renewal: interarrival times; renewal theorem for long-term behavior</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Karlin and Taylor, A First Course in Stochastic Processes</li>\n<li>Rogers and Williams, Diffusions, Markov Processes and Martingales</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch16/58-df-omega.md","status":"resolved","id":"5045d216c83e75cb","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-omega.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)","display":false},{"tex":"T\\in\\{\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\}","display":false},{"tex":"(E,\\mathcal E)","display":false},{"tex":"X\\in(E^\\Omega)^T","display":false},{"tex":"A\\in\\mathcal E","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_A\\in(T\\cup\\{\\infty\\})^\\Omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{FirstPassageTime}_S(\\tau_A,X,A)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}first\\text{-}passage} \\vdash \\operatorname{FirstPassageTime}_S(\\tau_A,X,A) \\leftrightarrow T\\in\\{\\omega,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\}\\land X\\in(E^\\Omega)^T\\land A\\in\\mathcal E\\land\\tau_A\\in(T\\cup\\{\\infty\\})^\\Omega\\land\\forall\\omega_0\\in\\Omega\\;\\bigl(\\tau_A(\\omega_0)=\\inf(\\{t\\in T:X(t)(\\omega_0)\\in A\\}\\cup\\{\\infty\\})\\bigr)","display":true}],"bytes":1901,"backlinks":[{"id":"958dafb656cb78b0","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{FirstPassageTime}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ and $\\operatorname{FirstPassageTime}_S(\\tau_a,B,\\{a\\})$ (see [[../batch07/58-df-first-passage.md]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-534","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-first-passage.md|58-df-first-passage]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["5045d216c83e75cb"]}